                <pb facs="0276" n="180" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg180"/>

                <head>No. 96.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hunter to Mr. Foote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-10-23"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 23,
                        1879</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 9.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your dispatch No. 3, of
                    the 26th June last, which nominates Mr. Peter A. McKellar for appointment as
                    vice-consul of the United States at Valparaiso, I have to inform you that the
                    Department deems it advisable that another nomination should be made for that
                    office. It is preferred that an American citizen be named if practicable.</p>
                <p>Your dispatch No. 8, of August 22 last, has been received.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. HUNTER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Second Assistant
                            Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
